    "https://www.defiance.edu/employment-opportunities/#teacher-education-clinical-supervisors": {
      "title": "Teacher Education Clinical Supervisors",
      "description": "Teacher Education Clinical Supervisors. The Teacher Education program is seeking part-time clinical supervisors for teacher education students participating in 5-week practicum experiences and in 15-week student teaching experiences for the fall and spring semesters. Our licensure areas include early and middle childhood education, adolescent and young adult (core content areas), and intervention specialist mild-to-moderate (K-12). Clinical supervisors are required to make site visits during normal school hours and attend meetings and/or training sessions on campus. Requirements include a master’s degree in education and teaching experience in P-12 schools. A current teaching license within the areas indicated above is preferred. To apply, please complete this application and send it, along with a cover letter and resume, to the Defiance College Teacher Education Department at chiggins@defiance.edu . For further information contact the Teacher Education Office at 419-783-2323."
    },
    "https://www.defiance.edu/employment-opportunities/#general-information-for-part-time-faculty-positions": {
      "title": "General Information for Part-Time Faculty Positions",
      "description": "General Information for Part-Time Faculty Positions. Defiance College is often in need of qualified individuals for our part-time faculty pool. Format of classes is generally face-to-face and content areas of need vary from semester to semester. Part-time faculty are responsible for providing quality instruction to students through well-prepared classes, relevant assignments, fair and holistic assessment of learning, clear directives, and timely and helpful feedback. Applicants must hold a master’s degree (Ph.D. preferred) in a relevant field and professional or teaching experience is desirable. To apply for any of the current areas of need as noted below, send a cover letter identifying the teaching area of interest, vitae/resume, and the contact information of three professional references to employment@defiance.edu . COMPOSITION: The English Department seeks adjuncts to provide quality instruction for both freshmen and sophomore composition courses. Courses to be taught include Composition I and Composition II: Introduction to Literary Genres. MARKETING: The Business Department seeks adjuncts to provide instruction for general marketing courses. ACCOUNTING: The Business Department seeks adjuncts to provide instruction for general accounting courses."
    }
  },
